1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,838
Most AI agent demos die when the Wi-Fi does.

2
00:00:02,838 --> 00:00:09,224
This one ran for 24 hours on a single laptop, entirely offline, on Gemma 4 through Ollama.

3
00:00:09,224 --> 00:00:10,578
No hosted middleware.

4
00:00:10,578 --> 00:00:11,739
No per-token bill.

5
00:00:11,739 --> 00:00:13,739
No thoughts leaving the device.

6
00:00:13,739 --> 00:00:16,719
Microverse Battery is a multi-agent simulation.

7
00:00:16,719 --> 00:00:24,518
A society of personas — an Artisan, a Trader, immigrant Strangers, a Harvester — generates artifacts over a long tick loop.

8
00:00:24,518 --> 00:00:28,703
Every call goes through a single Ollama chat to one Gemma 4 model.

9
00:00:28,703 --> 00:00:29,908
There is no router.

10
00:00:29,908 --> 00:00:31,239
There is no fallback.

11
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:35,829
The single-model invariant lives in one line of config: gemma4:26b.

12
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:45,467
We use Ollama's JSON Schema structured output for the Trader's artifact ranking, and we explicitly suppress Gemma's reasoning channel so it never leaks into the output.

13
00:00:45,467 --> 00:00:48,794
24 hours of soaking, zero thinking-channel leaks.

14
00:00:48,794 --> 00:00:50,469
This is the live dashboard.

15
00:00:50,469 --> 00:00:54,317
It's a static HTML page — no JavaScript framework, no backend.

16
00:00:54,317 --> 00:00:59,839
Every artifact you see was generated on one Apple Silicon laptop over one wall-clock day.

17
00:00:59,839 --> 00:01:03,252
13,794 events.

18
00:01:03,252 --> 00:01:06,479
702 multi-author workshop entries.

19
00:01:06,479 --> 00:01:13,243
Six resident agents, three of them immigrant Strangers spawned by a Watchdog when the conversation got stale.

20
00:01:13,243 --> 00:01:14,104
Click into one.

21
00:01:14,104 --> 00:01:19,042
Here, Aki — the resident Artisan — proposes a parchment treatment for a shared scroll.

22
00:01:19,042 --> 00:01:23,119
A Stranger answers with a technique from her imagined coastal homeland.

23
00:01:23,119 --> 00:01:26,794
Another Stranger overlays a third approach from the arid plains.

24
00:01:26,794 --> 00:01:32,593
The Trader scored the aggregate workshop entry, the Harvester accepted it, the provenance is on disk.

25
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:38,795
This is what local multi-agent intelligence looks like when the substrate gives the model room to be social.

26
00:01:38,795 --> 00:01:42,887
The project earned five Architecture Decision Records along the way.

27
00:01:42,887 --> 00:01:45,895
Each one closed a bottleneck and exposed the next.

28
00:01:45,895 --> 00:01:47,701
The local-first runtime works.

29
00:01:47,701 --> 00:01:51,010
We documented a model-level limit instead of hiding it.

30
00:01:51,010 --> 00:01:54,019
Shared workshops solved the solo-agent bottleneck.

31
00:01:54,019 --> 00:01:56,847
Structural fixes raised throughput eight times.

32
00:01:56,847 --> 00:01:58,532
Multi-turn scenes ship next.

33
00:01:58,532 --> 00:02:10,714
Microverse Battery proves that the hard parts of multi-agent AI — durability, observability, governance, honest measurement — already work today on one laptop with Gemma 4 and Ollama.

34
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,435
No API key required, ever.

35
00:02:12,435 --> 00:02:13,428
Clone the repo.

36
00:02:13,428 --> 00:02:14,422
Pull the model.

37
00:02:14,422 --> 00:02:15,812
Run your own society.

